# L §2.3 (tally 2.1.2, issue #29): "The depth at a point is the number of brackets ( ), [ ] and { } open there (calls,
# keys and as if included) plus the ifs and the from and ties by terms it is inside". A read chained by `from` nests
# without a bracket staying open: here 8 links, and inside the 8th link's bal( the depth is 8 terms + 1 bracket = 9.
# (Before 2.1.2 refcore counted no link: 9 links parsed, and 300 crashed it with a RecursionError.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place acc: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

def z: money PLN = bal(acc, 2026-02-01) from bal(acc, 2026-01-01) from bal(acc, 2026-01-01) from bal(acc, 2026-01-01) from bal(acc, 2026-01-01) from bal(acc, 2026-01-01) from bal(acc, 2026-01-01) from bal(acc, 2026-01-01) from bal(acc, 2026-01-01)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-DEPTH ...
